  "interpretation": [
    "Ponding score is the percentile rank of positive filled-minus-original terrain depth. A deeper mapped bowl can produce a strong percentile without any storm simulation.",
    "Filled-surface height is the regional priority-flood spill surface, not observed standing water or a design water level.",
    "Stadium-envelope-outside-pitch includes stands, track and other surfaces; it is not a surveyed seating or roof polygon.",
    "OSM features reflect map edits in2026; the labelled2024DTM may represent different, older terrain. Survey date/method/vertical error and changes since acquisition remain unknown.",
    "No turf infiltration, field underdrains, pumps, inlet capacity, stadium engineering design or flood event observations are available in the screening inputs. The model therefore cannot establish actual stadium flood risk.",
    "No named stadium is removed or downweighted. Any index change requires a general, evidence-based method and consistent application."
